p the  magics TGI Fridays within about a year  period of time we had transformed that  Center into one that not only was the  community proud of but that they  supported in droves for the shopping  center for 22 made it a hundred percent  occupied we sold it for about 48 now  magic wanted to launch his own  investment fund one that could pull in  hundreds of millions from investors  willing to bet on the urban market he  partnered with Bobby Turner chairman and  CEO of Canyon Capital Realty Advisors  who thought it would be easy to raise  the money  his capitalization target was 300  million dollars  a sum that canyon thought could be  raised in six months magic knew better  Irvin looked at me and said wow I  thought I was teaming up with a smart  partner Bobby Turner is chairman and CEO  of Canyon Capital Realty Advisors he  knows Bobby this is gonna take two years  to raise a son because institutional  capital believes that urban communities  are lonely worthy of philanthropy for  government spending and they don't  understand the opportunities magic was  right for two years he and Turner criss  crossed the country the pitch was I know  the urban consumer I know what they want  what they need  I've already done a wonderful job of  driving ROI with the theaters and with  Starbucks and I can do the same here  this is just gonna give me a bigger  footprint I can gain scale and I promise  you that the the strategy is sound there  was a lot of people who who said some  tough thing we're never invested over  America you know and right in front of  me you know and why wouldn't we invest  in your people I look down and there was  Bourbons hand on my thigh  ripping with all of his might Ervin took  a deep breath composed himself and  looked at this individual and said what  I can tell you is that when we people  raise our fund  we will not be investing in your  people's communities and that really  epitomized magic grace under fire magic  and Turner's persistence finally paid  off the three hundred million dollar  Canyon Johnson fund launched in 2002  borrowing on the 300 million Canyon  Johnson was able to underwrite 1.5  billion dollars in inner-city projects  housing and commercial ventures in 13  states we thought that that billion  dollars or more was going to provide us  with with really an opportunity to  transform the quality of life and be a  significant tipping point in the right  direction for minority communities  across the country  magic splashes deal was close to home  in 2003 Canyon Johnson decided to gamble  on downtown LA and bought the  Transamerica Center a 32 story office  tower in a sketchy neighborhood not far  from the Staples Center where the Lakers  played 100 million in 200 million out  nice double on leverage and people saw  the light and other people followed he  was a pioneer nobody ever thought in  their wildest dreams that's a Canyon  Johnson fund would purchase the  Transamerica building and that  transaction actually opened the  floodgates for us our second fund took  us two and a half months to raise we  went back to the exact same investors  who invested was in the first fund they  looked at us and said here's six hundred  million dollars fun three literally took  us two and a half phone calls to raise 1  billion dollars no longer were the  canyon Johnson urban funds pioneers we  were the established go-to investor in  the urban market despite the growth  Canyon Johnson's urban investment ride  has not been entirely magical in one of  his investments in Brooklyn community  and union activists attacked Magic for  investing in luxury condos instead of  affordable housing and for not giving  all of his workers union benefits throw  me because first of all I am a union guy  my parents grew up both through the  Union so I love the unions and that  particular building was not a decision  we made we have a management company  that manages those buildings and they  made that decision  that hurts that hurts me personally it  hurts my brand so we had to jump on that  and make sure people understand that  that's not who I am  we do care about our workers and we want  them to have health benefits that's what  it's all about  [Music]  on November 7th 2011  Magic Johnson mark the anniversary of  his gut-wrenching announcement that he  was HIV positive hey I am 20 years later  Wow  what a blessing  I get up about 4:30 in the morning  stretch about 5:00 and then I either run  two or three miles or I do type O not  coming to the office I love the work all  day and night and then I have a great  family  you know cookie is a great wife and  three kids and I have two grandkids now  I got a great life and so that keeps me  going  magic cashed out of his ownership stake  in the LA Lakers and Starbucks in 2010  for an estimated 100 million dollars  according to the Los Angeles Times his  personal net worth is reported to be  half a billion dollars the hall-of-famer  made another big play when he announced  the launch of a new cable television  network aspire that will offer uplifting  images of African Americans combined  with his ownership of vibe magazine and  the TV show Soul Train Magic is poised  to add media mogul to his titles yes he  has made millions and millions of  dollars and I'm happy for him but he has  demonstrated as few others have that you  can do good and do well at the same time  I'm like okay how high can he go he's  gonna keep on going until he's ranked  number one billionaires who doesn't take  magics call that means he could get into  any company any boardroom any chairman  any CEO and at least have a conversation  and when you're sitting there talking to  him one-on-one  good luck saying no to him Los Angeles  Dodgers owner Frank McCourt couldn't say  no to magic when he led a group of  investors and their successful 2.15  billion dollar bid for the historic team  in March 2012 the group including  baseball executive Stan Caston  Guggenheim Partners mark Walter and  longtime friend Peter Guber  paid the largest price tag ever for a  sports franchise magic is now headed to  the owners box he'd be a terrific owner  because he he focuses on a lot of things  but he's not intimidated by I would say  the stardom of the players no matter who  you are if you haven't walked in their  shoes you tend to be intimidated  by celebrity and by stardom that's just  the way it is but not if you're Magic  Johnson even though he's really  successful now I think this paths gonna  be wider I think there's gonna be like a  freeway when he's when he's done magic  success of course has never been defined  entirely in dollars and cents minorities  we are at site still in touch people  because we didn't lie to so much  they haven't been lied to by me see and  they see that and they say we love Him  because he's bringing change in urban  America and I think that those hurts  just said to me Wow job well done kid  and I take it every single time  especially when when I put my heart and  soul and everything that I do and they  know that  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]
 

